cfasl-3 — Binary fasl loader/deserializer (plan-1-compact-fasl).

Read a cfasl file and evaluate its top-level forms.

WHAT
- `bocl_fasl_load(path)`: open, verify magic + format-version (major mismatch ->
  WARN and fall back to source, mirroring %CHECK-FASL-VERSION).
- Read the INTERN TABLE: for each entry intern the symbol ONCE in its named package
  (creating the package if the fasl carried a defpackage earlier — but package
  creation is a normal top-level form in the stream, so most symbols' packages
  already exist by the time they are referenced; order the intern table AFTER the
  packages, or intern lazily on first reference).  Build the index->symbol array.
- Read the CONSTANT POOL into an index->object array.
- Read the FORM STREAM: for each form, deserialize the object graph (resolving
  symbol-refs / constant-refs / backrefs against the arrays), then evaluate it
  through the normal evaluator (evale / the %REPL-EVAL wrapper) so EVAL-WHEN and
  side effects behave exactly as a loaded source form.
- Rooting: the index arrays and the in-progress object must be pinned across the
  eval of each form (eval can GC).

KEY WIN: no reader (no character-level parse of huge s-exprs), no re-macroexpansion
(forms are already macro-free), and each symbol interned exactly once.

ACCEPTANCE: load a fasl produced by cfasl-2 and get identical definitions/effects to
loading the source; round-trip the corpus from cfasl-2.

DEPENDS ON: cfasl-1, cfasl-2.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DONE (v1.6.3, cfasl branch).

Implemented in two layers:

sources/cfasl.c — the pure deserializer (mirror of the cfasl-2 writer):
  cfasl_rctx* cfasl_rctx_new(cfasl_in*);
  Ref         cfasl_read_object(cfasl_rctx*);   -- rebuild one object graph
  int         cfasl_rctx_error(cfasl_rctx*);
  void        cfasl_rctx_free(cfasl_rctx*);
An id->object array mirrors the writer's shared-object table so BACKREFs resolve;
containers are recorded (cons/string/simple-vector) or reserve their id
(symbol/keyword/uninterned/ratio) BEFORE their sub-components, so cycles and
shared structure reconstruct with the ORIGINAL eq identity.  Symbols are
INTERNED (package_intern_cstring_in in the recorded package / KEYWORD_Package),
never copied, so a deserialized symbol is EQ to the live one — the "intern each
symbol once" win.  Uninterned symbols are freshly made (symbol_new).

sources/bocl.c — bocl_fasl_load(path), the binary counterpart of
bocl_load_cstring: reads the whole file, checks the "BOCLFASL" magic + u8
version (mismatch -> WARN to stderr + return NIL so LOAD falls back, mirroring
%CHECK-FASL-VERSION), binds *LOAD-PATHNAME*/*LOAD-TRUENAME* identically, then
loops reading + evaluating one top-level form per live-pool frame (bocl_eval, or
%LOAD-EVAL-TOPLEVEL-FORM under bocl_load_recover).  Per-form pools keep GC scans
O(form) not O(file), exactly as the text loader; definitions survive via their
symbols.  Returns T on success, NIL on not-a-cfasl / version mismatch, and warns
+ NIL on a truncated/malformed stream.

DESIGN NOTE (deviation from the sketch): the format has NO separate intern-table
/ constant-pool sections — cfasl-1 chose a single STREAMING shared-object id
space, so the loader is just deserialize-graph + eval, with interning happening
inline on first symbol occurrence (idempotent).  The shared-object scope is ONE
top-level form (fresh rctx per form): this bounds retention and mirrors the text
loader's per-form discipline, at the cost of re-emitting a cross-form-repeated
symbol's name once per form.  The dominant wins — no character-level reader, no
re-macroexpansion, within-form dedup, one intern per occurrence — are preserved;
the writer resets per form (cfasl-4) to keep the id numbering in sync.

ACCEPTANCE: tests/test_misc.c::
  - test_cfasl_roundtrip  — writer->reader is EQUAL to the source graph and
    preserves EQ (the two X of (setq x x) are one symbol, EQ to the interned X;
    char/ratio/keyword/simple-vector round-trip).
  - test_cfasl_load_file  — a full on-disk image (magic+version+DEFUN+EOF) loaded
    via bocl_fasl_load defines the function with real effect ((%cfasl-sq 7)=>49),
    and a non-cfasl file returns NIL for fallback.
Full suite: see the cfasl-3 commit (green).
